# Round fxbox (card for the dump_mtp rebuild): `just build-ref-dump-mtp`, the one build that every dump_mtp user (the glm5next and the
# qwen4exp MTP dumps, real and fixture) is stale on. The record /root/bloomery-data/bin/dump_mtp.build names the sha256 prefix
# 2260539a888c of the cpp and ref_tensor_io.h it was built from (commit a2c2484b0); main's tools/ref/dump_mtp.cpp plus
# ref_tensor_io.h hash to 66b0d36c9d88 (the same as this tree's), so dump-mtp.sh refuses the installed binary (rc 3) and the rebuild is the
# fix, not a tree-local change. The ik tree's libllama and libcommon are current against its HEAD (cmake --build finds nothing to
# do, 5-30 s), then g++ of dump_mtp.cpp against them (20-60 s) and an atomic replace of the binary: 0.5-1.5 min [derived from
# glmmtpref-dump.card's two-run decomposition]. Should cmake rebuild ik after all (CUDA objects), the hold is its ~10-15 min and
# the run's log says so; the lease's `minutes` band below is the first case's. Nothing is timed. After it:
# `dump_mtp.build` names 66b0d36c9d88 (read back), and the real sets on disk are untouched (the rebuild writes only bin/).
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_mtp's compile and the cmake check of ik's libraries use every core; beside a timed run or a gate batch it would take
  their cores, so the build holds the lease; why now: dump_mtp.cpp moved on main after the installed binary was built (record
  2260539a888c, source 66b0d36c9d88), so no MTP dump can start until it is rebuilt, and fxb's glmq2k dump and every later MTP set wait on it
minutes: 0.5..15
